tags: device-memory, vram

The memory of one device that the instance can use: for example the memory of a GPU.
It is a total for the device, not for the instance.

The value is in bytes. Example: 25769803776 (24 GiB).

An absent value says nothing (it is not 0). Valid only in the resources of a device
(Device.resources, DeviceChange, AttachedDevice). A node refuses it in the resources
of a container. The node reserves the value on the device and enforces it.

=== formal
class=resource
measure=the memory of one device that the instance can use at one time, as a total for the device
name=device-memory
place=the resources of a device
unit=byte
